      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you triggered a backend relabel sweep that processes many traces at once, the system now also runs the newer Opus 4 model alongside Sonnet for those full-file-context relabels, instead of being hardcoded to Sonnet only. The model name is built dynamically per trace, and any errors during the run now include the error's message and stack trace in the logs to make debugging faster. This affects only the admin-level bulk relabel pipeline that iterates over traces, not the regular per-user assistant experience.",
