        "v": 5,
        "title": "Enforce explicit deletion comments in edit snippets",
        "summary": "Strengthened prompting for `write_file` to mandate explicit deletion comments (e.g., `// Delete Block 2`) within edit snippets. This ensures the downstream 'fast-apply' model correctly interprets removals, as it cannot infer deletions from context alone. Updated `backend/src/tools.ts` to include detailed examples and stricter formatting rules for `content` parameters. Also corrected `updateSubgoal` status enum from 'ABORTED' to 'FAILED' in schema definitions.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T14:26:03.168Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you ask an AI assistant to edit a file, it now must add an explicit comment (like '// Delete Block 2') wherever you want code removed. This helps a secondary, simpler model that applies your edits understand what to cut out, since it can't infer deletions from context alone. You don't see this directly, but it makes edits less likely to accidentally leave behind or remove the wrong lines.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
