        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add isSubdir helper for cross-platform path checks",
        "summary": "Introduced `isSubdir` in `project-files.ts` to standardize directory containment checks. The function resolves paths and adds a Windows-specific drive letter comparison to prevent false positives across different drives. `menu.ts` and `terminal.ts` now use this helper instead of inline `path.relative` logic.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T14:24:47.219Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You're less likely to see a wrong-side-of-the-track warning when running commands on Windows. The app now checks which drive a folder lives on before deciding whether one folder sits inside another, so a folder on your C: drive won't be mistaken for one on D:. Nothing looks different otherwise, but the path checks used in the menu greeting and in the terminal are now using a shared, Windows-aware method instead of each doing its own guesswork.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
